// source: se-tests/gather.cpp, gather<T>() (sum += data[index[i]]), kept
//   out of line: float gather<float>(...) at 0x1f60, double
//   gather<double>(...) at 0x2120; the warm-up and the ROI pass call the
//   same function.
// registers: x1 = the index pointer (post-incremented), x0 = data,
//   w2/x2 = index[i].
// arrays: each thread's data and index are vectors of run<T>(), inlined
//   into main(); the relations are data[index]0 (float) and
//   data[index]1 (double).
// The index load is post-indexed, a macro-op in gem5 (see gapbs_pr).
offset: 0
